WEBVTT

00:02.200 --> 00:04.690
Scoring back when they score on me is my football!

00:04.690 --> 00:11.190
<i>The final match of the Tokyo Prefectural Tournament,
Toho Academy vs. Musashi Middle School, has become a head-on battle.</i>

00:11.690 --> 00:16.000
<i>Musashi brings Misugi into the game earlier than planned</i>

00:16.000 --> 00:20.250
<i>against Kojiro, who got a 3-goal lead
immediately after the start of the game.</i>

00:20.250 --> 00:24.920
Football is not only about individual skills—
team-play is also important, Hyuga.

00:25.630 --> 00:29.800
<i>He immediately steals a goal from Toho Academy
as soon as he enters the game,</i>

00:29.800 --> 00:32.300
<i>overwhelming them with his magnificent play.</i>

00:32.300 --> 00:34.630
I've got you—now the lead drops to one!

00:35.680 --> 00:38.430
I won't let you score again!

00:38.430 --> 00:42.900
<i>The one who stopped the surging Misugi
was the goalkeeper, Wakashimazu.</i>

00:42.900 --> 00:46.280
<i>With a super save, he manages to prevent another goal.</i>

00:46.280 --> 00:48.110
<i>That's Wakashimazu for you.</i>

00:48.110 --> 00:51.200
<i>Quick, explosive agility and jumping skill.</i>

00:51.200 --> 00:53.610
<i>It looks like I won't be able to score from long range.</i>

00:54.640 --> 00:56.360
<i>The first half ends here.</i>

00:57.560 --> 01:00.900
That was a close call! They were just about to score.

01:00.900 --> 01:05.870
Isn't Misugi great? He instantly changed the game's atmosphere.

01:05.870 --> 01:11.250
He's also just so cool. They are right
to call him the Young Noble of the Field.

01:13.720 --> 01:17.590
Of course, Tsubasa is much cooler than him.

01:17.590 --> 01:19.740
That's beyond any doubt.

01:19.740 --> 01:23.350
He's so very cool, but Misugi is just so...

01:23.350 --> 01:27.990
Kumi, do you even know why you are watching this match?

01:27.990 --> 01:29.480
Of course I do!

01:29.480 --> 01:34.220
To get to know the opponents we might play against, we watch these games and record them.

01:34.220 --> 01:35.360
It's fine if you do.

01:35.360 --> 01:38.140
Oh, I need to tell everyone!

01:43.030 --> 01:46.090
What? So Misugi came out to play in the first half?

01:46.090 --> 01:46.770
Yes.

01:46.770 --> 01:47.580
Wow...

01:47.580 --> 01:50.280
Then, who knows what will happen in the second half...

01:54.260 --> 01:56.970
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:54.260 --> 01:56.970
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:57.880 --> 02:00.550
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

01:57.880 --> 02:00.550
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:01.470 --> 02:04.180
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:01.470 --> 02:04.180
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:11.060 --> 02:13.900
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

02:11.060 --> 02:13.900
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

02:13.900 --> 02:20.160
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

02:13.900 --> 02:20.160
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

02:20.160 --> 02:26.040
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

02:20.160 --> 02:26.040
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

02:26.040 --> 02:32.630
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

02:26.040 --> 02:32.630
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

02:32.630 --> 02:36.630
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

02:32.630 --> 02:36.630
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

02:36.630 --> 02:41.140
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

02:36.630 --> 02:41.140
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

02:41.140 --> 02:46.680
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

02:41.140 --> 02:46.680
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

02:46.680 --> 02:48.270
<i>baka darou?</i>

02:46.680 --> 02:48.270
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

02:48.270 --> 02:49.480
<i>ai</i>

02:48.270 --> 02:49.480
<i>Love!</i>

02:49.480 --> 02:52.980
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

02:49.480 --> 02:52.980
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

02:52.980 --> 03:02.870
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

02:52.980 --> 03:02.870
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

03:02.870 --> 03:03.700
<i>ai</i>

03:02.870 --> 03:03.700
<i>Love!</i>

03:03.700 --> 03:07.500
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

03:03.700 --> 03:07.500
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

03:07.500 --> 03:11.500
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

03:07.500 --> 03:11.500
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

03:11.500 --> 03:17.760
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

03:11.500 --> 03:17.760
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

03:17.760 --> 03:20.550
<i>hanasanai</i>

03:17.760 --> 03:20.550
<i>for a single moment!</i>

03:22.220 --> 03:27.220
<b><b>EPISODE 33: <b>
CONCLUSION OF TOKYO TOURNAMENT</b></b></b>

03:22.520 --> 03:25.180
All right! The first half wasn't half bad.

03:25.180 --> 03:27.930
Don't worry about the goal you conceded to Misugi.

03:27.930 --> 03:31.840
In the second half, as part of our anti-Misugi tactic, Sawada will mark him.

03:31.840 --> 03:32.690
Yes!

03:32.690 --> 03:37.190
Wait a second, coach. Please let me mark Misugi.

03:37.190 --> 03:42.240
I'll get my payback in the second half. I'll tackle him and steal the ball from him.

03:42.240 --> 03:44.200
Just calm down, Hyuga.

03:44.200 --> 03:47.180
Football is a competitive game where you fight as a team.

03:47.180 --> 03:49.870
You only have to complete the tasks given to you.

03:49.870 --> 03:56.130
As a center forward, you will stay in front and aim to score with counter-attacks.

03:56.130 --> 03:59.990
You can't hope to play well if you get too fixed on with what's in front of you.

03:59.990 --> 04:01.730
Got it, Hyuga?

04:01.730 --> 04:02.630
Yes.

04:03.220 --> 04:04.360
<i>Damn it!</i>

04:04.360 --> 04:06.880
<i>It's true, football's a contest between the teams...</i>

04:06.880 --> 04:11.190
<i>But it's equally important to have a one-on-one match as a man!</i>

04:11.190 --> 04:14.520
<i>What kind of match is this, where you can't settle your score with a rival...?</i>

04:14.520 --> 04:21.350
Hyuga, our goal is to prevent Nankatsu's third victory at the Nationals and to become champions.

04:21.350 --> 04:24.800
To do that, we absolutely need to win this match.

04:24.800 --> 04:25.660
So, please...

04:27.180 --> 04:28.790
I know that too well, Takeshi.

04:28.790 --> 04:29.790
Hyuga...

04:32.820 --> 04:35.590
We gave up 3 goals at the start, but now we are pushing them.

04:35.590 --> 04:37.490
Keep it up in the second half!

04:37.490 --> 04:38.130
Yes!

04:38.130 --> 04:42.610
And Misugi, you'll only play until the 20th minute.

04:42.610 --> 04:44.120
I know.

04:44.120 --> 04:46.520
We'll turn the tables before then, Misugi!

04:46.520 --> 04:48.590
Let's go to the Nationals!

04:48.590 --> 04:49.360
Yes!

04:49.360 --> 04:50.140
Guys!

04:52.460 --> 04:54.310
<i>20 minutes more...</i>

04:55.120 --> 04:57.310
<i>Both teams' players step out onto the field.</i>

04:58.020 --> 05:01.820
<i>After the first half, the score is 3-1 and Toho is in the lead,</i>

05:01.820 --> 05:05.070
<i>but thanks to Misugi, the game's moving at Musashi's pace.</i>

05:05.070 --> 05:08.070
<i>Will Toho manage to protect this score?</i>

05:08.820 --> 05:11.950
<i>We can't tell how this final match will end!</i>

05:11.950 --> 05:15.080
<i>The second half starts with Musashi Middle School's kick-off!</i>

05:18.710 --> 05:20.430
<i>The ball gets to Misugi!</i>

05:20.430 --> 05:23.590
<i>Misugi has been scoring all alone since the first half.</i>

05:23.590 --> 05:27.300
<i>Sawada immediately moves to steal the ball from Misugi.</i>

05:27.300 --> 05:33.060
<i>To block Musashi's attacks, we can't let Misugi move freely.</i>

05:33.060 --> 05:33.560
Suzuki!

05:33.560 --> 05:36.080
<i>Misugi passes the ball here.</i>

05:36.080 --> 05:37.810
<i>All right, this is going well.</i>

05:42.900 --> 05:45.130
<i>Musashi is exchanging passes in the back.</i>

05:45.130 --> 05:47.660
<i>They haven't moved to attack their opponent's side at all.</i>

05:47.660 --> 05:50.280
<i>Come, I'll protect here and then counter-attack.</i>

05:50.280 --> 05:52.830
<i>I'll return the goal you stole from us back at you.</i>

05:52.830 --> 05:54.330
Captain!

05:54.330 --> 05:56.160
<i>The ball gets to Misugi once again.</i>

05:56.950 --> 05:59.540
<i>But Sawada follows him right away.</i>

05:59.540 --> 06:01.630
<i>It appears that I won't be able to dribble.</i>

06:01.630 --> 06:02.520
<i>If that's the case...</i>

06:02.520 --> 06:04.340
<i>A long pass from Misugi.</i>

06:04.340 --> 06:05.410
Okay.

06:05.410 --> 06:08.130
<i>Will Musashi be able to shoot in one go?</i>

06:08.130 --> 06:09.640
That's too naive!

06:10.940 --> 06:14.720
<i>But goalkeeper Wakashimazu jumps out and firmly catches the ball.</i>

06:15.320 --> 06:17.730
<i>Toho's defense is strong, just like I expected.</i>

06:20.150 --> 06:21.360
Okay, come on!

06:22.300 --> 06:24.780
<i>Toho's ace Hyuga dashes away on a fast break!</i>

06:24.780 --> 06:26.490
<i>It's time for their counter-attack!</i>

06:27.320 --> 06:28.030
Captain!

06:29.030 --> 06:29.740
All right!

06:34.360 --> 06:37.180
<i>Oh, he's offside!</i>

06:37.180 --> 06:38.280
What...?

06:38.280 --> 06:41.750
<i>It's Musashi and Misugi's favorite trick, the offside trap!</i>

06:41.750 --> 06:42.790
Damn it!

06:42.790 --> 06:44.400
<i>The game goes back and forth!</i>

06:44.400 --> 06:46.460
<i>A fierce offense and defense continues!</i>

06:46.920 --> 06:50.430
<i>Misugi has the upper hand over Sawada in keeping possession,</i>

06:50.430 --> 06:52.970
<i>and Musashi is superior in number of attacks,</i>

06:54.860 --> 06:58.220
<i>but time and time again, Wakashimazu won't yield to them!</i>

06:58.220 --> 07:00.140
Nice catch, Wakashimazu!

07:02.460 --> 07:06.480
<i>Thanks to their offside trap, Musashi hasn't given Toho any chance to score.</i>

07:07.130 --> 07:08.110
Damn it!

07:09.240 --> 07:13.530
<i>Both teams can't finish their attacks, and every passing moment is a moment wasted.</i>

07:15.050 --> 07:17.560
Even though we're attacking this much, we can't score!

07:17.560 --> 07:20.210
It's almost time to pull Misugi back.

07:20.210 --> 07:22.210
It's almost time.

07:22.210 --> 07:25.210
We can't push him too much in this heat.

07:30.550 --> 07:34.230
<i>I have to score another goal soon, and close this 2-goal gap!</i>

07:35.700 --> 07:37.680
<i>Wakashimazu is a renown goalkeeper.</i>

07:37.680 --> 07:42.190
<i>If I can't create a decisive position like I did in the first goal, I can't score.</i>

07:42.670 --> 07:43.270
Honma!

07:43.270 --> 07:45.160
<i>A short pass from Misugi.</i>

07:45.160 --> 07:47.070
<i>Will they get in front with a one-two?</i>

07:47.070 --> 07:48.820
It's no use, Misugi!

07:50.820 --> 07:51.400
Take this!

07:52.870 --> 07:53.700
All right!

07:53.700 --> 07:56.230
<i>Wakashimazu was tricked into going to the wrong side!</i>

07:56.230 --> 07:58.700
<i>The tall Sanada runs forward!</i>

07:58.700 --> 08:00.040
I've got this!

08:00.040 --> 08:02.160
<i>This is an absolute chance!</i>

08:02.160 --> 08:04.420
Like I'd let you!

08:05.420 --> 08:07.500
<i>But this is useless too!</i>

08:07.500 --> 08:09.800
<i>Wakashimazu punches this away!</i>

08:10.880 --> 08:12.130
<i>Okay, that's it!</i>

08:12.900 --> 08:16.350
<i>Misugi is dashing to the loose ball!</i>

08:16.350 --> 08:20.440
<i>Before Sawada catches up, I will shoot while the ball is still high.</i>

08:20.440 --> 08:21.350
<i>And for that...</i>

08:21.930 --> 08:23.600
<i>This is my only option!</i>

08:27.640 --> 08:33.400
<i>Misugi jumps while running, turning his body for an overhead!</i>

08:33.400 --> 08:34.360
What?!

08:36.160 --> 08:38.410
Go!

08:38.410 --> 08:39.410
Captain!

08:40.040 --> 08:43.540
<i>Wakashimazu is still off-balance!</i>

08:43.540 --> 08:44.670
Wakashimazu!

08:44.670 --> 08:47.670
Do you think that I'll let them score any more against <i>me</i>?

08:51.090 --> 08:52.270
<i>It's in!</i>

08:52.270 --> 08:55.140
<i>Misugi steals his second goal off of Wakashimazu!</i>

08:55.140 --> 08:56.220
<i>Damn it!</i>

08:58.220 --> 09:00.000
You did it, captain!

09:00.000 --> 09:00.720
All right!

09:00.720 --> 09:03.460
<i>Still, Misugi is impressive.</i>

09:03.460 --> 09:06.520
<i>He pulled out such a bold overhead kick here and now!</i>

09:06.520 --> 09:07.480
A second goal...

09:07.480 --> 09:10.950
<i>He displayed great ball control
and got it to the right corner of the goal.</i>

09:10.950 --> 09:12.490
All right, I did it!

09:13.990 --> 09:15.840
You did it, Misugi!

09:15.840 --> 09:17.630
Finally, the lead is down to one!

09:19.420 --> 09:21.490
Captain!

09:21.490 --> 09:24.700
Oh no! We are over Misugi's 30-minutes time limit!

09:24.700 --> 09:26.230
Nishiyama, we'll sub you in right now!

09:26.230 --> 09:27.080
Okay.

09:27.080 --> 09:28.960
Please wait, coach!

09:30.150 --> 09:31.260
Captain...

09:34.970 --> 09:37.490
I'm okay. I can still play.

09:39.050 --> 09:40.810
Captain...

09:41.260 --> 09:42.640
Just another goal...

09:42.640 --> 09:45.880
Tying the score is the least I should do for the team.

09:45.880 --> 09:48.540
Please, give me another chance.

09:48.540 --> 09:49.480
But Misugi...

09:49.880 --> 09:51.400
It'll be okay.

09:51.400 --> 09:56.990
I had a chance to rest during half-time, and I know my body the best.

09:57.820 --> 10:00.480
Just another chance...

10:00.480 --> 10:01.620
Misugi...

10:01.620 --> 10:03.620
I'm begging you, coach!

10:05.190 --> 10:06.250
Got it.

10:07.840 --> 10:10.920
Thank you so much, coach.

10:12.520 --> 10:18.350
<i>I thought Musashi would sub Misugi after the planned 30 minutes, but I was wrong.</i>

10:18.350 --> 10:20.980
<i>Misugi will keep on playing.</i>

10:20.980 --> 10:22.300
What is the meaning of this?

10:22.300 --> 10:25.270
How can they ignore my orders as his doctor?

10:25.270 --> 10:27.860
It'll be dangerous for him to play any longer.

10:27.860 --> 10:32.190
Please doctor, please let him play!

10:32.900 --> 10:38.320
<i>Captain has undergone a very harsh rehab for 2 years just to play in this tournament.</i>

10:38.320 --> 10:42.620
<i>He staked everything on his last tournament in middle school,</i>

10:43.290 --> 10:45.790
<i>so that he could play against Tsubasa once more.</i>

10:46.520 --> 10:47.660
<i>Tsubasa...</i>

10:48.910 --> 10:51.130
So doctor, I'm begging you!

10:51.860 --> 10:53.380
You...

10:54.180 --> 10:55.710
<i>What's wrong, Kojiro?</i>

10:55.710 --> 11:00.180
<i>You could only play in the first half when Misugi wasn't in the game.</i>

11:00.780 --> 11:06.060
<i>Misugi scored 2 goals in 30 minutes, but you scored 3 just in 50 minutes.</i>

11:06.060 --> 11:11.460
<i>You are clearly losing the duel between you and Misugi, Kojiro.</i>

11:11.460 --> 11:12.560
Damn it all.

11:12.560 --> 11:14.680
<i>This can't go on like this.</i>

11:14.680 --> 11:18.490
<i>If Misugi keeps playing, we'll be swept by their pace.</i>

11:18.490 --> 11:21.660
<i>If it's come to this, we should aim for another goal.</i>

11:21.660 --> 11:23.240
<i>Sawada, go on the offensive!</i>

11:24.410 --> 11:27.840
Hyuga, I just got the sign to join the attack.

11:27.840 --> 11:29.290
Let's aim for another goal.

11:29.290 --> 11:30.460
You bet we will!

11:31.370 --> 11:33.710
<i>My football consists solely of offense.</i>

11:33.710 --> 11:35.840
<i>It's football only when you attack.</i>

11:35.840 --> 11:38.320
<i>Don't get too carried away, Misugi.</i>

11:38.320 --> 11:40.900
<i>I'll show you how I play football now.</i>

11:50.020 --> 11:53.020
<i>Toho's lead has been cut to a single goal,</i>

11:53.020 --> 11:57.610
<i>and Sawada has moved to offense to help shake Musashi off once again.</i>

12:00.190 --> 12:03.530
<i>I'm counting on you... Captain, Takeshi.</i>

12:05.250 --> 12:06.560
Let's go, Takeshi!

12:06.560 --> 12:07.400
Yes!

12:07.400 --> 12:10.960
<i>Toho attacks with their ace Hyuga and Sawada as the focus!</i>

12:10.960 --> 12:14.330
<i>Will Musashi be able to fend this attack off?</i>

12:14.330 --> 12:17.920
All right guys! Let's stop them here and tie the game!

12:17.920 --> 12:18.590
Right!

12:22.210 --> 12:24.820
<i>Two of Musashi's players try to steal the ball!</i>

12:24.820 --> 12:26.510
<i>Will he pass the ball to Sawada?</i>

12:26.510 --> 12:29.010
I, alone, am enough for you weaklings!

12:30.960 --> 12:32.760
<i>No, he breaks through by himself!</i>

12:32.760 --> 12:35.850
<i>Has Hyuga's fierce spirit made its return?</i>

12:35.850 --> 12:37.520
<i>Here I come Musashi!</i>

12:37.520 --> 12:43.360
<i>If I bring the ball all the way up myself, your offside trap won't work!</i>

12:43.360 --> 12:45.440
I will mark Hyuga.

12:45.440 --> 12:48.440
When I get the ball, let's go for a quick counter-attack!

12:48.440 --> 12:48.910
Yeah!

12:49.910 --> 12:55.330
<i>Hyuga and Misugi are finally going for a one-on-one battle at this late part of the game!</i>

12:55.940 --> 12:59.840
<i>That's how I want it! Let's go Misugi!</i>

12:59.840 --> 13:01.480
<i>Come at me, Hyuga!</i>

13:01.480 --> 13:04.840
<i>If I stop you, we can definitely tie the game!</i>

13:12.790 --> 13:16.980
<i>Misugi approaches from the side to stop Hyuga's dribble.</i>

13:16.980 --> 13:18.730
<i>Hyuga is keeping the ball.</i>

13:18.730 --> 13:21.360
<i>It's a fierce battle between them!</i>

13:27.420 --> 13:30.120
<i>Will Hyuga be able to move inside?</i>

13:30.750 --> 13:33.000
<i>Or will Misugi cut him off?</i>

13:33.000 --> 13:35.460
Go for it, Hyuga!

13:35.460 --> 13:37.460
Misugi!

13:42.800 --> 13:45.510
<i>It looks like Hyuga is not considering a pass.</i>

13:45.510 --> 13:47.130
Hyuga...

13:47.810 --> 13:50.090
<i>Damn it, I can't shake him off at all!</i>

13:50.090 --> 13:51.420
<i>What's up with this guy?!</i>

13:51.420 --> 13:52.220
<i>I will pass you!</i>

13:53.740 --> 13:54.220
<i>I will st–</i>

13:58.380 --> 13:59.060
Misugi!

13:59.060 --> 14:00.060
Captain!

14:00.060 --> 14:00.940
Misugi!

14:00.940 --> 14:01.690
Misugi!

14:02.180 --> 14:04.760
<i>What's happening to Misugi?!</i>

14:04.760 --> 14:07.700
<i>He falls suddenly as if he was trying to lean on Hyuga!</i>

14:09.040 --> 14:10.490
<i>Guys...</i>

14:13.540 --> 14:14.500
<i>What?!</i>

14:15.000 --> 14:18.420
<i>Misugi nudges the ball away even as he's falling to the ground!</i>

14:18.420 --> 14:19.410
All right!

14:19.410 --> 14:21.710
<i>Musashi recovers this loose ball!</i>

14:23.420 --> 14:25.340
Everyone, follow Misugi's orders!

14:25.340 --> 14:26.630
It's a fast counter-attack!

14:26.630 --> 14:27.420
Okay!

14:27.420 --> 14:29.760
<i>A counter-attack for Musashi!</i>

14:29.760 --> 14:32.810
<i>Toho quickly returns to defend in reply!</i>

14:32.810 --> 14:34.180
Come back to defense guys!

14:34.760 --> 14:36.930
<i>This is a chance Misugi created for us.</i>

14:36.930 --> 14:40.230
<i>A chance he created by risking his life.</i>

14:40.230 --> 14:44.730
<i>We'll follow Misugi's orders and make it count!</i>

14:45.140 --> 14:46.240
<i>Come at me, you weaklings!</i>

14:46.240 --> 14:49.570
<i>As if I'd let anyone else but Misugi score!</i>

14:49.570 --> 14:52.740
<i>This will be the moment for this match, y'know.</i>

14:52.740 --> 14:55.120
<i>5 minutes remain.</i>

14:55.120 --> 14:59.120
<i>This match is reaching its peak at this moment!</i>

14:59.840 --> 15:00.370
Sanada!

15:00.920 --> 15:01.630
Honma!

15:02.420 --> 15:03.620
<i>Here it goes!</i>

15:03.620 --> 15:07.050
<i>A perfectly combined passing march of Musashi without trapping the ball.</i>

15:07.050 --> 15:09.170
A long shot won't work against Wakashimazu!

15:09.170 --> 15:12.550
We will advance to the goal as close as we get,

15:12.550 --> 15:17.640
create the perfect opportunity, and shoot!

15:17.640 --> 15:18.310
Okay!

15:18.310 --> 15:23.310
<i>Musashi's forwards are advancing relentlessly, as if Misugi's fighting spirit passed on to them!</i>

15:23.770 --> 15:26.470
<i>Toho's defenders can't react at all!</i>

15:26.470 --> 15:27.570
What are you doing?!

15:27.570 --> 15:30.740
<i>Musashi is just in front of the goal!</i>

15:30.740 --> 15:32.070
<i>Come if you want!</i>

15:32.070 --> 15:33.700
I'm leaving it to you, Honma!

15:33.700 --> 15:37.420
<i>There goes the last pass from Musashi.</i>

15:37.420 --> 15:39.420
That's a score, y'know.

15:39.420 --> 15:40.960
A perfect opportunity.

15:42.500 --> 15:48.840
I, Ken Wakashimazu, will give up on playing football if I let you score the third one here!

15:48.840 --> 15:51.250
<i>Wakashimazu makes a zealous dash!</i>

15:51.250 --> 15:54.550
<i>But Honma is ready to shoot!</i>

15:54.550 --> 15:56.550
I got it!

15:58.470 --> 15:59.310
What?!

16:01.910 --> 16:04.020
<i>This is—</i>

16:06.000 --> 16:09.560
<i>He stopped him! Wakashimazu!</i>

16:09.560 --> 16:11.140
You did it, Wakashimazu!

16:11.140 --> 16:12.360
Blocked him nicely!

16:12.360 --> 16:15.980
<i>After a mad dash, he stopped him with both hands,</i>

16:15.980 --> 16:19.910
<i>preventing himself from being blown out had he just used one!</i>

16:19.910 --> 16:21.460
Wakashimazu!

16:21.460 --> 16:26.600
<i>Musashi attacked fiercely to capitalize on the chance Misugi gave them,</i>

16:26.600 --> 16:31.250
<i>but Wakashimazu persevered, determined to not give up a third goal.</i>

16:31.250 --> 16:33.130
<i>Wakashimazu is the winner here!</i>

16:33.130 --> 16:37.190
<i>Musashi couldn't turn this perfect situation into a goal.</i>

16:37.190 --> 16:38.960
<i>Great, well done.</i>

16:38.960 --> 16:40.890
<i>Now this game is ours.</i>

16:41.810 --> 16:44.390
<i>Referee stops play here.</i>

16:44.390 --> 16:47.620
<i>Is Misugi, who fell to ground earlier, okay?</i>

16:47.620 --> 16:49.600
Captain!

16:49.600 --> 16:50.590
I am okay.

16:50.590 --> 16:51.320
Misugi.

16:51.740 --> 16:52.900
Did you score?

16:54.190 --> 16:55.910
Sorry.

16:56.860 --> 16:58.410
Is that so?

16:58.410 --> 16:59.940
We can't let him play any further!

16:59.940 --> 17:01.680
Nishiyama, get ready, quick!

17:01.680 --> 17:02.250
Yes, sir!

17:02.830 --> 17:05.750
<i>Misugi finally goes out.</i>

17:05.750 --> 17:09.750
<i>He returns to the bench with his teammate helping him out.</i>

17:10.260 --> 17:11.630
Captain.

17:14.220 --> 17:15.830
Jun, dear!

17:15.830 --> 17:16.720
Misugi!

17:19.050 --> 17:20.780
Do your best, guys!

17:20.780 --> 17:23.140
There are still a few minutes left.

17:23.750 --> 17:25.740
Do not give up until the very end!

17:25.740 --> 17:26.650
Sure!

17:29.630 --> 17:35.750
<i>Misugi, the Young Noble of the Field, silently leaves the pitch in the middle of the game.</i>

17:35.750 --> 17:38.530
<i>He really did a great job until now.</i>

17:38.530 --> 17:40.110
<i>Here goes Jun Misugi!</i>

17:40.110 --> 17:41.370
Misugi...

17:43.730 --> 17:47.960
<i>After having Misugi substituted, Musashi Middle School fought vigorously,</i>

17:48.300 --> 17:51.640
<i>but led by Kitazume, Toho's defense was thick.</i>

17:52.540 --> 17:55.080
<i>Good, don't do anything unnecessary.</i>

17:55.080 --> 17:57.260
<i>Keep passing and make the time tick away.</i>

17:57.260 --> 17:58.760
<i>Understood.</i>

17:58.760 --> 18:01.100
<i>There is a little time left.</i>

18:01.100 --> 18:03.440
<i>Musashi's done all they could.</i>

18:03.440 --> 18:04.520
<i>Guys...</i>

18:06.640 --> 18:07.970
Like we'd give up!

18:07.970 --> 18:08.940
Hyuga!

18:10.520 --> 18:11.520
Hyuga!

18:17.030 --> 18:19.110
<i>This whistle marks the end of the match!</i>

18:19.110 --> 18:19.790
We did it!

18:19.790 --> 18:24.200
<i>Toho Academy's gotten their National Tournament ticket 3rd time in a row!</i>

18:28.250 --> 18:29.170
All right.

18:31.520 --> 18:33.710
It was close, Misugi.

18:33.710 --> 18:34.590
Yeah.

18:35.760 --> 18:40.330
<i>I couldn't play against Tsubasa in these 3 years after all.</i>

18:43.000 --> 18:45.520
The Tokyo Tournament is over.

18:45.520 --> 18:48.980
Toho has won the game, 3-2.

18:48.980 --> 18:50.610
One goal difference, huh?

18:50.610 --> 18:51.750
That was a close one.

18:51.750 --> 18:52.940
3-2.

18:53.760 --> 18:57.360
<i>It seems it is Toho and Kojiro Hyuga this year, once again.</i>

19:01.080 --> 19:03.950
Congratulations on your victory Coach Kitazume.

19:03.950 --> 19:07.400
What's your goal after getting a ticket
to the Nationals for a third time in a row?

19:07.400 --> 19:09.290
We aim to become champions, of course.

19:09.290 --> 19:13.670
With our current strength, I am sure we can defeat Nankatsu.

19:13.670 --> 19:17.910
Sawada's addition to the team was effective indeed.

19:19.230 --> 19:21.200
Coach Kira.

19:21.200 --> 19:26.010
Kojiro, you sure have gotten soft in the time we haven't seen each other.

19:27.600 --> 19:28.850
Championship pennant, huh?

19:29.620 --> 19:32.670
I can't believe such a thing is enough to make you happy.

19:34.110 --> 19:38.360
You're just a caged, defanged tiger, now!

19:41.420 --> 19:43.740
Defanged tiger?

19:43.740 --> 19:45.580
That's right.

19:45.580 --> 19:47.580
Don't you get it, Kojiro?

19:47.580 --> 19:50.710
You've become way too soft after going to Toho.

19:51.520 --> 19:55.790
Even though you were on the pitch, you felt pity for Misugi.

19:55.790 --> 20:00.190
Because of that, you lost the ball, allowed them to make a counter-attack,

20:00.190 --> 20:03.370
and to top that all of, you couldn't even go back to defend.

20:03.370 --> 20:05.370
sudden realization

20:05.850 --> 20:09.750
It all worked out due to Wakashimazu's excellent play,

20:09.770 --> 20:14.000
but if they had tied the game, the responsibility would've been yours.

20:15.270 --> 20:19.400
I don't remember teaching you such football, Kojiro!

20:19.400 --> 20:22.790
Throw away your mercy once you get on the field!

20:22.790 --> 20:25.220
What you need to have is harshness!

20:25.220 --> 20:31.040
If it were the old you, you'd aim for the goal even if it meant smashing Misugi's heart!

20:31.040 --> 20:34.040
A case for mouri kogoro

20:34.040 --> 20:40.680
After being accepted to Toho, you've been able to focus on football, without worrying about anything else.

20:40.680 --> 20:44.700
As a result, it seems that you seem
to have lost most of your hunger,

20:44.700 --> 20:48.390
which has put out your burning fighting spirit.

20:48.800 --> 20:51.220
You weren't like this, back then.

20:51.220 --> 20:55.650
Despite your circumstances, you pushed them aside to become strong.

20:57.610 --> 20:59.030
<i>It's about time.</i>

20:59.030 --> 21:02.290
<i>Do your practices properly even if I am not here.</i>

21:02.290 --> 21:04.030
<i>Yes, Captain!</i>

21:04.030 --> 21:06.700
KONAKA HOSPITAL

21:08.410 --> 21:09.950
<i>Wakashimazu!</i>

21:09.950 --> 21:11.310
<i>Captain.</i>

21:11.310 --> 21:13.790
<i>You didn't need to visit me at all.</i>

21:13.790 --> 21:14.550
<i>It's no big deal.</i>

21:14.550 --> 21:17.210
<i>I just dropped by on my way back from work.</i>

21:17.940 --> 21:18.950
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>

21:18.950 --> 21:22.990
<i>Make sure you recover well from that injury by the National Tournament!</i>

21:22.990 --> 21:23.920
<i>Captain...</i>

21:23.920 --> 21:27.910
That's why all of them followed your lead.

21:28.560 --> 21:33.440
Takeshi and Wakashimazu followed you
and joined Toho, but as you are now,

21:33.440 --> 21:37.980
neither them nor the rest of your team
would follow you anywhere.

21:37.980 --> 21:46.540
You won't be able to reach that Tsubasa Ozora who's steadily advancing towards his dreams.

21:50.600 --> 21:55.580
I opened a football school in Okinawa, and I'm coaching there.

21:55.580 --> 22:00.840
If you don't want to lose for a third
time in a row against Tsubasa Ozora...

22:00.840 --> 22:03.440
...no, a fourth time, if you add elementary school,

22:03.440 --> 22:05.800
you're welcome to come any time you want.

22:11.630 --> 22:12.720
Hyuga.

22:38.790 --> 22:44.840
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.790 --> 22:44.840
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.840
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.840
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.840 --> 22:56.890
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.840 --> 22:56.890
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.890 --> 23:01.520
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.890 --> 23:01.520
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:07.820
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:07.820
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.150 --> 23:15.240
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.150 --> 23:15.240
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.240 --> 23:21.290
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:25.750
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:25.750
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.050 --> 23:33.390
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.050 --> 23:33.390
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.390 --> 23:39.430
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.430 --> 23:45.730
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.430 --> 23:45.730
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.070 --> 24:00.720
COMING UP, EPISODE 34:
THE CURTAIN RAISES ON THE FIERCE BATTLE!
THE TOURNAMENT STARTS!
